  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Finite flat surjections are surjective on $k$-points",
  "statement": "Let $k$ be algebraically closed and $f:X\\to Y$ a finite flat\nsurjective morphism of schemes of finite type over $k$. Then\n$f(X(k))=Y(k)$.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-abelian-varieties/sk-prop-av-divisible/lem-sc-finite-flat-surj-points.md",
    "place": "node lem-sc-finite-flat-surj-points, order 571"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "Let $y\\in Y(k)$. The fibre $X_y=X\\times_Yy$ is nonempty\n(surjectivity), finite and flat over $k$, hence a nonempty finite\n$k$-scheme, which has a $k$-point by\n[lem-sc-finite-nonempty-point]; such a point is an\n$x\\in X(k)$ with $f(x)=y$.",
      "uses": [
        "lem-sc-finite-nonempty-point"
      ],
      "elementary": false
    }
  ],
